WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.790
An invented Wellington HR team wants a
new starter checklist they can reuse,

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.350
written the same way every time.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.910
Three Claude features help with that job.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.310
A Project holds reusable
instructions and reference material.

5
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.710
A file supplies evidence.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.150
An Artifact gives you separate output,

7
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.590
to revise beside the conversation.

8
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.110
Start with the job, not every button.

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.070
Keep your notes beside the draft,

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:32.270
so every step can be traced back
to something you actually supplied.

11
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.470
First, the Project.

12
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.350
Open Projects, then New Project.

13
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.070
Call it Practice office emails.

14
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.950
Free accounts can create
up to five Projects.

15
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.630
Keep this one private.

16
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.470
Choose Set project instructions,

17
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.590
and add a few short rules.

18
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.430
Use New Zealand English.

19
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.750
Use only the supplied facts.

20
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.070
Flag missing dates and owners.

21
00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.430
Keep everything as a draft
for a person to review.

22
00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.190
One detail. The Project's name and
description aren't context Claude can read.

23
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.550
Put the rules you need
in the instructions,

24
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.550
and the reference facts in
the Project's knowledge.

25
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.030
On Team and Enterprise plans, Projects
can be shared inside the organisation.

26
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.150
So check who can see a Project
before you add anything to it.

27
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.870
Next, evidence. In a chat,
choose the plus button,

28
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.270
then Add files or photos.

29
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.150
Attach the tiny practice
file from the lesson:

30
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.550
invented notes for a painting job.

31
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.390
Ask for the scope, the exclusions,

32
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.150
the proposed start, and anything missing.

33
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.190
Then compare every line with the file.

34
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.830
The notes say the start is
subject to client approval,

35
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:49.190
and the price is not yet confirmed.

36
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.910
So the summary must keep
the approval condition,

37
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.310
and must not invent a price.

38
00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.910
Now, the output. Ask for a simple
checklist Artifact for the new starter.

39
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.470
Artifacts need Cloud code execution
and file creation turned on,

40
00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.550
in Settings, Capabilities.

41
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.430
Your organisation may manage that setting.

42
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.310
Chat Artifacts work on every plan,

43
00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.750
Free included. The Design, Slides and
Docs templates are only on paid plans,

44
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.510
and you won't need them here.

45
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.910
If it isn't available, ask for
the checklist in the chat instead.

46
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.710
Then ask for one revision, and replace
any invented staff name with an owner

47
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.750
placeholder. A checklist that invents
who's responsible isn't finished.

48
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.990
That's the pattern: prepare, ask,

49
00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.950
check, approve. Finish
with a short handover note:

50
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.230
which source you used, what you checked,

51
00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.230
and what's still uncertain.

52
00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.870
Claude Code and other advanced
tools are topics for later training.

53
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.150
For now, complete one small office task.

54
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.150
The useful result is the one you
can trace back to its source.
